  <section class="section container">
    <h2>Key takeaways</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>UAE duty and VAT compound to ×1.1025: on a US$10,000 CIF the add is US$500 duty + US$525 VAT = US$1,025 (10.25%), not 10%. That US$25 VAT-on-duty gap is the compounding trap.</li>
      <li>Chargeable weight adds 66.7% on the light carton: 60 × 50 × 40 cm ÷ 6,000 = 20 kg against 12 kg actual, an 8 kg uplift. At AED 20–23.5/kg that is AED 8 × 20 = AED 160 to AED 8 × 23.5 = AED 188 of extra bill.</li>
      <li>The ÷5,000 divisor makes the same carton 20% heavier: 120,000 ÷ 5,000 = 24 kg versus 120,000 ÷ 6,000 = 20 kg, a 4 kg uplift. At AED 20–23.5/kg that adds AED 80–94 — ask which divisor each quote uses.</li>
      <li>Air is 2.0–2.7× sea LCL on a 100 kg comparison: 100 kg at AED 20–23.5/kg = AED 2,000–2,350, while 1 CBM LCL is AED 880–980. AED 2,000 ÷ AED 980 = 2.04 and AED 2,350 ÷ AED 880 = 2.67, but kg and CBM are not the same basis.</li>
      <li>Air's speed is 2.1–10× sea, but dangerous goods can cancel it: 15–30 days sea divided by 3–7 days air gives 30 ÷ 3 = 10× at the top and 15 ÷ 7 = 2.14× at the bottom. An undeclared lithium battery can stop the shipment before it boards.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

